  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multi-profile, PCA-2000, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) is the current best at 0.619 acc, showing that multimodal fusion with avgpool aggregation adds ~0.028 over the best RNA-only config (config_002, 0.591). The fusion method (concat vs weighted) is the only untested dimension within this exact architecture. Question: Does weighted fusion outperform simple concatenation when combining PCA-encoded RNA with ResNet50 image features under avgpool aggregation? This is a clean single-variable A/B test against config_018. Why best next: Under a limited budget, confirming or ruling out the fusion mechanism before investing in more expensive architectural changes (ViT-L, scvi, scgpt) is the most information-efficient step. A positive result gives an immediate improvement to the best config; a null result cleanly eliminates a design axis and redirects effort toward higher-impact choices like image encoder quality or RNA encoder nonlinearity."
}

